      "text": "Recognising first aorist forms",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 19,
      "bbox": [
        349,
        187,
        396,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": 139,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "When you encounter an aorist indicative form in a reading passage, you will at times be faced with a challenge. In order to look a verb up, you will have to ascertain its dictionary form (i.e. the first person s. present indicative).",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 1,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 20,
      "bbox": [
        412,
        211,
        428,
        321
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Simple stems",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "■",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 21,
      "bbox": [
        435,
        218,
        467,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Sometimes this process is simple, since it will require only the removal of the augment, σ and personal ending, e.g.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 2,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 22,
      "bbox": [
        483,
        218,
        500,
        310
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἐκέλευσε:",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 3,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 23,
      "bbox": [
        510,
        218,
        523,
        442
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(a) remove augment = κελευσε",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 4,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 24,
      "bbox": [
        526,
        218,
        539,
        531
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(b) Remove σε (3s. ending) = κελευ-",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 5,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 25,
      "bbox": [
        542,
        218,
        578,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(c) κελευ- is the stem. Therefore the verb is κελεύω, ‘I order’. Translation:\n‘he/she/it ordered’.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 6,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 26,
      "bbox": [
        595,
        211,
        610,
        338
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Complex stems",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "■",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 27,
      "bbox": [
        617,
        187,
        664,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": 140,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "On other occasions, however, the process will be more complex. For example, it may not be immediately clear what the final consonant of the stem would be in the present, e.g.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 7,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 28,
      "bbox": [
        679,
        218,
        696,
        310
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἔβλεψα:",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 8,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 29,
      "bbox": [
        705,
        218,
        718,
        483
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(a) Remove augment = βλεψα",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 9,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 30,
      "bbox": [
        721,
        218,
        735,
        608
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": 31,
      "text": "(b) Remove σα (1s. ending) = what stem?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 10,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 32,
      "bbox": [
        743,
        83,
        913,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "• It might be ψ-, from the verb βλέψ-ω. Look it up – no such verb.\n• But βλεψ- might have been produced by a combination of β or π or πτ or φ + σ.\n• The stem could therefore be any of βλεβ-, βλεπ-, βλεπτ- or βλεφ- .\n• If so, the verb could be βλέβω, βλέπω, βλέπτω or βλέφω.\n• If you recognise βλέπω, ‘I look (at)’, you will translate ἔβλεψα ‘I looked at’.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    }
